The attached image (Figure 5) illustrates how Nano-11 facilitates antigen transport to draining lymph nodes. Panel A shows flow cytometry plots detailing the detection and phenotyping of OVA+ cells in draining lymph nodes on Day 1 and Day 2 following injection with soluble OVA, OVA+aluminum hydroxide (AH), or OVA+Nano-11. Nano-11 (OVA+N11) significantly increased the mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) of OVA in OVA-containing cells on both days compared to soluble OVA and OVA+AH (Panel B), indicating enhanced antigen uptake per cell. Panel C further demonstrates that Nano-11 significantly increased the percentage of migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) among OVA-positive cells, highlighting its effectiveness in targeting antigens to these critical antigen-presenting cells.